IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `nsw-interpretation-time`
IMPORT `nsw-p5-construction`
IMPORT `nsw-seat`

-- Interpretation Act 1987 (New South Wales) -- WORKED CASES for the seat layer (nsw-seat.l4).
-- Every question of the seat layer has at least one case here, and each case states the facts a person in the seat would state.
-- The expected value beside each case is worked out by hand from the text, with the section that decides it. A case that expects NOTHING is a case the Act does not answer.
-- Dates: the first day of a period dating from a given day is the next day (s 36(1)); "month" is a calendar month (Schedule 4); the Act does not define "day", "week" or "year".

-- The days a House sat, used for the sitting-day cases (the sample stands in for the borrowed fact, which the Act does not state): 3 to 18 March 2026, sixteen days in a row.
`the sample sitting days` MEANS LIST (Date 3 3 2026), (Date 4 3 2026), (Date 5 3 2026), (Date 6 3 2026), (Date 7 3 2026), (Date 8 3 2026), (Date 9 3 2026), (Date 10 3 2026), (Date 11 3 2026), (Date 12 3 2026), (Date 13 3 2026), (Date 14 3 2026), (Date 15 3 2026), (Date 16 3 2026), (Date 17 3 2026), (Date 18 3 2026)

`no holidays` MEANS EMPTY

§ `Counting a period of time`

-- Thirty days from 1 January 2026: the first day counted is 2 January, so the thirtieth day is 31 January (a Saturday).
#ASSERT `On which day does my period end` (Date 1 1 2026) PeriodOfDays 30 EQUALS JUST (Date 31 1 2026)
-- Two months from 31 December 2025: the first month is 1 to 31 January, the second 1 to 28 February 2026 (a Saturday).
#ASSERT `On which day does my period end` (Date 31 12 2025) PeriodOfMonths 2 EQUALS JUST (Date 28 2 2026)
-- One month from 31 January 2024: the month begins on 1 February and ends on 29 February 2024 (a leap year).
#ASSERT `On which day does my period end` (Date 31 1 2024) PeriodOfMonths 1 EQUALS JUST (Date 29 2 2024)
-- One month from 15 January 2025: the month begins on 16 January and ends immediately before 16 February, so on 15 February.
#ASSERT `On which day does my period end` (Date 15 1 2025) PeriodOfMonths 1 EQUALS JUST (Date 15 2 2025)
-- One month from 28 February 2025: the month begins on 1 March and ends on 31 March.
#ASSERT `On which day does my period end` (Date 28 2 2025) PeriodOfMonths 1 EQUALS JUST (Date 31 3 2025)
-- The Act does not define "year" or "week": three years from 16 July 2025, five years from 15 January 2025 and from 1 September 2025, one year from 29 February 2024, and a period of weeks, are not covered.
#ASSERT `On which day does my period end` (Date 16 7 2025) PeriodOfYears 3 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `On which day does my period end` (Date 15 1 2025) PeriodOfYears 5 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `On which day does my period end` (Date 1 9 2025) PeriodOfYears 5 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `On which day does my period end` (Date 29 2 2024) PeriodOfYears 1 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `On which day does my period end` (Date 1 1 2026) PeriodOfWeeks 2 EQUALS NOTHING
-- A calendar year is a period of 12 months commencing on 1 January: one calendar year from 31 December 2024 starts on 1 January 2025 and ends on 31 December 2025; one from 10 March 2025 does not start on 1 January.
#ASSERT `On which day does my period end` (Date 31 12 2024) PeriodOfCalendarYears 1 EQUALS JUST (Date 31 12 2025)
#ASSERT `On which day does my period end` (Date 10 3 2025) PeriodOfCalendarYears 1 EQUALS NOTHING

-- Thirty days from 1 January 2026 end on Saturday 31 January; the first following day that is not a Saturday, a Sunday or a holiday is Monday 2 February 2026.
#ASSERT `By which day must I act` (Date 1 1 2026) PeriodOfDays 30 `no holidays` EQUALS JUST (Date 2 2 2026)
-- the same, with Monday 2 February 2026 a public holiday in the place: Tuesday 3 February 2026
#ASSERT `By which day must I act` (Date 1 1 2026) PeriodOfDays 30 (LIST (Date 2 2 2026)) EQUALS JUST (Date 3 2 2026)
-- Two months from 31 December 2025 end on Saturday 28 February; Monday 2 March 2026.
#ASSERT `By which day must I act` (Date 31 12 2025) PeriodOfMonths 2 `no holidays` EQUALS JUST (Date 2 3 2026)
-- One month from 31 January 2024 ends on Thursday 29 February 2024, a day that counts as it is.
#ASSERT `By which day must I act` (Date 31 1 2024) PeriodOfMonths 1 `no holidays` EQUALS JUST (Date 29 2 2024)
-- Ten days from Monday 2 March 2026 end on Thursday 12 March; a holiday on 12 March moves the day to Friday 13 March 2026.
#ASSERT `By which day must I act` (Date 2 3 2026) PeriodOfDays 10 `no holidays` EQUALS JUST (Date 12 3 2026)
#ASSERT `By which day must I act` (Date 2 3 2026) PeriodOfDays 10 (LIST (Date 12 3 2026)) EQUALS JUST (Date 13 3 2026)
-- three years from 16 July 2025: not covered
#ASSERT `By which day must I act` (Date 16 7 2025) PeriodOfYears 3 `no holidays` EQUALS NOTHING

-- The given day is not counted (section 36(1)); the thirtieth day is.
#ASSERT `Is the day I am asking about inside my period of days` (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 31 1 2026) 30 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is the day I am asking about inside my period of days` (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 2 1 2026) 30 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is the day I am asking about inside my period of days` (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) 30 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is the day I am asking about inside my period of days` (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 2 2026) 30 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- a period of one and a half days is not a period the Act speaks of
#ASSERT `Is the day I am asking about inside my period of days` (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 2 1 2026) 1.5 EQUALS NOTHING

-- section 36(3): the power to extend may be exercised, and an application for an extension made, after the period has expired
#ASSERT `Can I still apply for an extension after my period has run out` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I still apply for an extension after my period has run out` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Can I still apply for an extension after my period has run out` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I still apply for an extension after my period has run out` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I still apply for an extension after my period has run out` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- Monday 5 January 2026 is a working day and a business day; Saturday 3 January is neither; a listed holiday is neither.
#ASSERT `Is the day I am asking about a working day` (Date 5 1 2026) `no holidays` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Is the day I am asking about a working day` (Date 3 1 2026) `no holidays` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Is the day I am asking about a working day` (Date 4 1 2026) `no holidays` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Is the day I am asking about a working day` (Date 5 1 2026) (LIST (Date 5 1 2026)) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Is the day I am asking about a business day` (Date 5 1 2026) `no holidays` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Is the day I am asking about a business day` (Date 3 1 2026) `no holidays` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Is the day I am asking about a business day` (Date 6 1 2026) (LIST (Date 6 1 2026)) EQUALS FALSE

§ `When an Act or a statutory rule takes effect`

-- Nothing else provides (section 23(1)(a)): assent on 10 June 2026, so the 28th day after is 8 July 2026.
#ASSERT `On which day does the Act commence` (Date 10 6 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST (Date 8 7 2026)
-- The Act names its day (section 23(1)(b)): 1 September 2026.
#ASSERT `On which day does the Act commence` (Date 10 6 2026) TRUE (Date 1 9 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 1 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST (Date 1 9 2026)
-- A proclamation under the Act appoints 1 August 2026 and is published on 20 July 2026, before that day (section 23(1)(b)).
#ASSERT `On which day does the Act commence` (Date 10 6 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) TRUE (Date 1 8 2026) (Date 20 7 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST (Date 1 8 2026)
-- the same, published on 5 August 2026, after that day: the Act commences on the day the proclamation is published (section 23(5)(a))
#ASSERT `On which day does the Act commence` (Date 10 6 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) TRUE (Date 1 8 2026) (Date 5 8 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST (Date 5 8 2026)
-- The Act is silent and the Governor appoints 20 June 2026 by a proclamation published 15 June (section 23(2)).
#ASSERT `On which day does the Act commence` (Date 10 6 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) TRUE (Date 20 6 2026) (Date 15 6 2026) TRUE EQUALS JUST (Date 20 6 2026)
-- the same, published on 25 June, after that day: the earlier of the publication day and the day it would have commenced without the proclamation, 8 July (section 23(5)(b))
#ASSERT `On which day does the Act commence` (Date 10 6 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) TRUE (Date 20 6 2026) (Date 25 6 2026) TRUE EQUALS JUST (Date 25 6 2026)
#ASSERT `On which day does the Act commence` (Date 10 6 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) TRUE (Date 20 6 2026) (Date 20 7 2026) TRUE EQUALS JUST (Date 8 7 2026)
-- a day appointed under section 23(2) outside the 28 days is not covered
#ASSERT `On which day does the Act commence` (Date 10 6 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) TRUE (Date 15 8 2026) (Date 1 8 2026) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING


-- section 39: a rule published on 5 March 2026 that specifies no day, a later day (1 April) or an earlier day (1 March)
#ASSERT `On which day does the statutory rule commence` (Date 5 3 2026) FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) EQUALS Date 5 3 2026
#ASSERT `On which day does the statutory rule commence` (Date 5 3 2026) TRUE (Date 1 4 2026) EQUALS Date 1 4 2026
#ASSERT `On which day does the statutory rule commence` (Date 5 3 2026) TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) EQUALS Date 5 3 2026
#ASSERT `On which day does the statutory rule commence` (Date 5 3 2026) TRUE (Date 5 3 2026) EQUALS Date 5 3 2026

-- section 24: an Act or statutory rule commencing on 1 July 2026 has commenced at the beginning of that day, which is the end of 30 June
#ASSERT `Has the Act or statutory rule commenced at the moment I am asking about` AnAct (Date 1 7 2026) (Date 1 7 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Has the Act or statutory rule commenced at the moment I am asking about` AStatutoryRule (Date 1 7 2026) (Date 30 6 2026) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Has the Act or statutory rule commenced at the moment I am asking about` AnAct (Date 1 7 2026) (Date 29 6 2026) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Has the Act or statutory rule commenced at the moment I am asking about` AnAct (Date 1 7 2026) (Date 30 6 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- another instrument is not covered by section 24
#ASSERT `Has the Act or statutory rule commenced at the moment I am asking about` AnotherInstrument (Date 1 7 2026) (Date 1 7 2026) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- section 71: an Act expressed to expire on 30 June 2026 continues in operation until the end of that day
#ASSERT `Is the Act or instrument still operating at the moment I am asking about` (Date 30 6 2026) (Date 30 6 2026) FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Is the Act or instrument still operating at the moment I am asking about` (Date 30 6 2026) (Date 29 6 2026) TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Is the Act or instrument still operating at the moment I am asking about` (Date 30 6 2026) (Date 30 6 2026) TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Is the Act or instrument still operating at the moment I am asking about` (Date 30 6 2026) (Date 1 7 2026) FALSE EQUALS FALSE

-- section 30D: a repeal on 1 July 2026 takes effect at the beginning of that day
#ASSERT `Has the repeal taken effect at the moment I am asking about` (Date 1 7 2026) (Date 1 7 2026) FALSE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Has the repeal taken effect at the moment I am asking about` (Date 1 7 2026) (Date 30 6 2026) TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Has the repeal taken effect at the moment I am asking about` (Date 1 7 2026) (Date 30 6 2026) FALSE EQUALS FALSE

§ `Repeals and what continues`

-- section 29: the new provisions commence on 1 July 2026
#ASSERT `Are the repealed provisions still in force on the day I am asking about` TRUE (Date 1 7 2026) (Date 30 6 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Are the repealed provisions still in force on the day I am asking about` TRUE (Date 1 7 2026) (Date 1 7 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Are the repealed provisions still in force on the day I am asking about` FALSE (Date 1 7 2026) (Date 30 6 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- section 30C: assent 1 March 2020, last provision commences 10 March 2020; or the Act commenced before assent; or it makes provision for its own repeal; or it was enacted before 2009
#ASSERT `On which day is the amending Act repealed` (Date 1 3 2020) (Date 10 3 2020) FALSE EQUALS JUST (Date 11 3 2020)
#ASSERT `On which day is the amending Act repealed` (Date 1 3 2020) (Date 1 2 2020) FALSE EQUALS JUST (Date 2 3 2020)
#ASSERT `On which day is the amending Act repealed` (Date 1 3 2020) (Date 10 3 2020) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `On which day is the amending Act repealed` (Date 1 3 2008) (Date 10 3 2008) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Statutory rules in Parliament`

-- section 40(4): a notice not laid in accordance with section 40 does not affect the operation of the rule; where it was laid in accordance with it, the section is silent
#ASSERT `Does the statutory rule I rely on stop working if the written notice was not laid before Parliament in time` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does the statutory rule I rely on stop working if the written notice was not laid before Parliament in time` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- section 41(1)(b): the notice was laid on 3 March; the 15th sitting day after is 18 March
#ASSERT `Until which day can notice of a motion to disallow the statutory rule still be given` `the sample sitting days` (Date 3 3 2026) EQUALS JUST (Date 18 3 2026)
#ASSERT `Until which day can notice of a motion to disallow the statutory rule still be given` `the sample sitting days` (Date 10 3 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Can the statutory rule I rely on still be disallowed` `the sample sitting days` TRUE (Date 3 3 2026) (Date 18 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can the statutory rule I rely on still be disallowed` `the sample sitting days` TRUE (Date 3 3 2026) (Date 19 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- before the notice is laid, a House may pass a resolution at any time (section 41(1)(a))
#ASSERT `Can the statutory rule I rely on still be disallowed` `the sample sitting days` FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) (Date 1 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE

§ `Serving a document by post`

-- Posted on Thursday 1 January 2026: the seventh working day after is Monday 12 January 2026 (2, 5, 6, 7, 8, 9 and 12 January).
#ASSERT `On which day is the document I posted taken to have been served` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) `no holidays` EQUALS JUST (Date 12 1 2026)
-- with Tuesday 6 January 2026 a public holiday in the place: Tuesday 13 January 2026
#ASSERT `On which day is the document I posted taken to have been served` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) (LIST (Date 6 1 2026)) EQUALS JUST (Date 13 1 2026)
-- evidence sufficient to raise doubt displaces the deeming; a letter posted elsewhere is not covered by section 76(1)(b)
#ASSERT `On which day is the document I posted taken to have been served` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE (Date 1 1 2026) `no holidays` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `On which day is the document I posted taken to have been served` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) `no holidays` EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Forms`

#ASSERT `Is it enough that I substantially followed the form` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is it enough that I substantially followed the form` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Age and minors`

-- born 15 March 2008: 18 on 15 March 2026
#ASSERT `On which day does the person attain the age` (Date 15 3 2008) 18 EQUALS JUST (Date 15 3 2026)
-- born 29 February 2008: 16 on 29 February 2024 (a leap year); 18 would be 29 February 2026, which does not exist, and the Act does not say what then
#ASSERT `On which day does the person attain the age` (Date 29 2 2008) 16 EQUALS JUST (Date 29 2 2024)
#ASSERT `On which day does the person attain the age` (Date 29 2 2008) 18 EQUALS NOTHING
-- a minor is under 18: still a minor at the end of 13 March 2026, not at the end of 14 March (the same instant as the beginning of 15 March)
#ASSERT `Is the person a minor at the moment I am asking about` TRUE (Date 15 3 2008) (Date 13 3 2026) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is the person a minor at the moment I am asking about` TRUE (Date 15 3 2008) (Date 14 3 2026) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is the person a minor at the moment I am asking about` TRUE (Date 15 3 2008) (Date 15 3 2026) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is the person a minor at the moment I am asking about` FALSE (Date 15 3 2008) (Date 13 3 2026) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Measuring a distance`

#ASSERT `How is the distance measured` AnActPassedBeforeTheCommencementOfThisAct EQUALS JUST "along the nearest route ordinarily used in travelling"
#ASSERT `How is the distance measured` AnInstrumentMadeUnderAnActPassedBeforeTheCommencementOfThisAct EQUALS JUST "along the nearest route ordinarily used in travelling"
#ASSERT `How is the distance measured` AnActPassedAfterTheCommencementOfThisAct EQUALS JUST "in a straight line on a horizontal plane"
#ASSERT `How is the distance measured` AnInstrumentMadeUnderAnActPassedAfterTheCommencementOfThisAct EQUALS JUST "in a straight line on a horizontal plane"
#ASSERT `How is the distance measured` SomeOtherPurposeOfMeasuringDistance EQUALS NOTHING
